From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: screen sharing for Linux apps

Linux apps (OBS, browsers, Discord, AnyDesk) share the screen through the
ScreenCast portal, whose NickelOS backend publishes it as a PipeWire
stream. ChromeOS has no way to hand the screen to a process outside
Chrome other than ARC's; this adds one for the backend, on
VmApplicationsService:

- NickelScreenCastChoose(app name, types): ChromeOS's own "share your
  screen" picker, as for ARC apps' screen capture (screens, and windows if
  asked), answering with the chosen DesktopMediaID and its size in pixels.
- NickelScreenCastStart(source, frame buffer, pipe, size, slots, cursor,
  app name): copies the screen's or window's layer (CopyOutputRequest,
  system memory) at most 30 times a second into the backend's shared
  memory, BGRx, and writes each frame's slot to the pipe; Ash draws the
  pointer into the frames when asked (as for ARC). ChromeOS's "is sharing
  your screen" notification stops it; so do the source going away and the
  pipe closing.
- NickelScreenCastStop(source).

